{"id":"b11","level":3,"levelName":"Ulpan Bet","n":15,"of":22,"title":"The ending that owns it","titleHe":"כִּנּוּיֵי קִנְיָן","goal":"Read בֵּיתוֹ and סְפָרָיו — possession hung on the back of the noun.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"שֶׁל is how possession is said out loud. There is a second way, older and shorter, which hangs the owner directly on the end of the noun — and it is everywhere in writing, so it has to be readable even if you never produce it."},{"type":"table","caption":"בַּיִת with endings","head":["","form"],"rows":[["my house","בֵּיתִי"],["your house (m.)","בֵּיתְךָ"],["your house (f.)","בֵּיתֵךְ"],["his house","בֵּיתוֹ"],["her house","בֵּיתָהּ"],["our house","בֵּיתֵנוּ"],["their house","בֵּיתָם"]]},{"type":"text","body":"The endings are the ones you already know from שֶׁל and from the prepositions — ־ִי me, ־ְךָ you, ־וֹ him, ־ָהּ her. What changes is the noun in front of them, which shifts to its construct shape first: בַּיִת becomes בֵּית־, and only then takes the ending."},{"type":"table","caption":"A plural noun takes a second set","head":["","form"],"rows":[["my books","סְפָרַי"],["your books (m.)","סְפָרֶיךָ"],["his books","סְפָרָיו"],["her books","סְפָרֶיהָ"],["our books","סְפָרֵינוּ"],["their books","סִפְרֵיהֶם"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"The tell for a plural noun with an owner is the yod before the ending — סְפָרַי, סְפָרָיו. Miss it and you have read a singular. It is the commonest silent mistake in a first year of reading."},{"type":"text","body":"A handful have survived into ordinary speech, where the long form would sound wrong: שְׁמִי my name, לְדַעְתִּי in my opinion, בְּיָדוֹ in his hand, and the family words אִשְׁתּוֹ his wife and בְּנוֹ his son."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"מַה שְּׁמֵךְ?","en":"What is your name? (to a woman)"},{"he":"הוּא כָּתַב אֶת דְּבָרָיו.","en":"He wrote down his words."},{"he":"לְדַעְתִּי, זֶה לֹא נָכוֹן.","en":"In my opinion, that isn't right."},{"he":"בֵּיתָם גָּדוֹל וְיָפֶה.","en":"Their house is big and beautiful."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"שְׁמִי","en":"my name","translit":"shmi"},{"he":"בֵּיתִי","en":"my house","translit":"beiti"},{"he":"בְּנוֹ","en":"his son","translit":"bno"},{"he":"אִשְׁתּוֹ","en":"his wife","translit":"ishto"},{"he":"יָדוֹ","en":"his hand","translit":"yado"},{"he":"לְדַעְתִּי","en":"in my opinion","translit":"leda'ti"},{"he":"דְּבָרָיו","en":"his words","translit":"dvarav"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["fridge","my name","consequently","pain"],"correct":1,"prompt":"שְׁמִי","translit":"shmi"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["my house","sleeps","enemy","a film, a ribbon"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בֵּיתִי","translit":"beiti"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["un-, without","explains","a curse","his son"],"correct":3,"prompt":"בְּנוֹ","translit":"bno"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["religion","his wife","sings","a little"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אִשְׁתּוֹ","translit":"ishto"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a connection","closed","his hand","receives, gets"],"correct":2,"prompt":"יָדוֹ","translit":"yado"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in my opinion","three (f.)","market","maybe"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לְדַעְתִּי","translit":"leda'ti"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["his words","wave","asks","cheese"],"correct":0,"prompt":"דְּבָרָיו","translit":"dvarav"},{"type":"choice","q":"our house?","options":["בֵּיתֵנוּ","בֵּיתְךָ","בֵּיתִי","בֵּיתֵךְ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"their house?","options":["בֵּיתְךָ","בֵּיתֵךְ","בֵּיתָם","בֵּיתִי"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “his hand”?","options":["שְׁמִי","חֻלְצָה","יִתְלַבֵּשׁ","יָדוֹ"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"his books?","options":["סְפָרֶיהָ","סְפָרַי","סְפָרֶיךָ","סְפָרָיו"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “his wife”?","options":["אִשְׁתּוֹ","מֶזֶג אֲוִיר","אֶתְמוֹל","שֵׁן"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"her house?","options":["בֵּיתָהּ","בֵּיתֵךְ","בֵּיתְךָ","בֵּיתִי"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["דְּבָרָיו","לְדַעְתִּי","אִשְׁתּוֹ","שְׁמִי"],"correct":2,"say":"אִשְׁתּוֹ","he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “his words”?","options":["כַּלָּה","שֹׁרֶשׁ","מוֹכֵר","דְּבָרָיו"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “his wife” in Hebrew","answer":"אִשְׁתּוֹ","hint":"ishto"}]}